Although I was playing for a streak here, my aim in games prior to this,
after ascending for the first time, was to ascend with the least number
of wishes used, without farming or loitering waiting for stuff to turn
up. So my games tend to be on the slow side, and often have either few
wishes used, or used for non-essential nice-to-have stuff just prior to
starting the ascension run (like grease, cursed gain level potions etc).

It is surprising how, with a little caution and creative use of kit,
many of the serious hazards for dying early on can be minimised. Shortly
before this streak, I lost a game killed by a wand of lightning
immediately on opening a door, which is the kind of death you just can't
avoid. Generally those out-of-your-hands deaths are quite rare, and the
more usual dangers - wand of fire on the ground in sokoban, say - can
be minimised by assuming it might happen and shoving pets in front, or
standing at corners so you at least meet it up close, etc.

My descriptions of ten ascensions would be nearly 100k, a bit big for a
Usenet post I think. So for the story of each ascension,
http://blog.moria.org.uk/games/nethack/yaasp . I'll just give a one-line
summary of each here:

#1) neutral male human Priest
Tough early game - there were several close calls, including down to 1hp
on one occasion. There was a magic lamp at Izchak's which did not give a
wish; in the end I ascended wishless and polyless.

#2) neutral male human Tourist
With a magic lamp from Izchak's I wished up Magicbane. Generally smooth
game.

#3) neutral male human Barbarian
Easy.

#4) lawful female dwarven Valkyrie
I'm a moron - I use an early wish for the PYEC, forgetting my alignment.
D'oh! Notwithstanding my best effort to mess up the game, it goes
smoothly from then on.

#5) cph, chaotic male human Wizard
The astral plane is fun in this game; a knight wielding Vorpal Blade is
in one of the sanctums, and has a charmed life - he kills almost
everything in the sanctum under conflict, dodges 5 or 6 death rays, so
ultimately I run round him. Otherwise a smooth game.

#6) neutral male human Monk
I wasn't thinking about the streak so much at the start of this game,
and instead wanted to keep weaponless and vegetarian; failed both (the
latter only on one occasion, d'oh). The early game was fraught, but
later I got 2 magic lamps and it went smoothly from there.

#7) lawful male human Knight
Generally tough game; I prayed in a tight spot in sokoban and my god was
displeased, and was saved by my horse. Oh so close. I didn't get either
MR or reflection in the early game, so the mid game was tricky too;
finally I found a dangerous bones on dlvl 20 with multiple dragons,
where I got an amulet of reflection, and a CoMR from a throne wish. And
then the ascension run had major problems - a mind flayer got randomly
summoned while I was putting on levitation boots, so it had two turns
before I could react, and hit me once; I forgot several scrolls and
wands and had to re-identify a lot of stuff on my way to the endgame.

#8) lawful male dwarven Caveman
Ah, my oriental caveman (I got gifted Snickersnee early on). I had
trouble getting reflection, and fought Ludios without it (if the
difference between bravery and foolishness is measured by success, on
this occasion it was brave). It went smoothly from there.

#9) chaotic female orcish Rogue
I'm starting to really like rogues. Straightforward game.

#10) lawful male human Samurai
I forgot to put numlock on and somehow killed my own pet on turn 3 -
ouch. Recovered though and no major problems after that.

